# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION PUBLIC CONFIG — committed on purpose
# =============================================================================
#
# ⚠  THIS FILE IS IN THE REPOSITORY. EVERY VALUE IN IT IS PUBLIC.
#
# It exists because Vite loads `.env.production` for `vite build` and
# `storybook build`, so CI and Vercel both pick these values up without them
# being duplicated into workflow YAML and a dashboard.
#
# ONLY `VITE_`-PREFIXED, GENUINELY PUBLIC VALUES BELONG HERE.
#
# Anything `VITE_` is inlined into the browser bundle and readable by anyone with
# devtools — so it must be safe to publish. Anything NOT prefixed `VITE_` is
# server-side: it does NOT belong in this file, because this file is committed.
#
# A guard enforces that: scripts/publish-to-github.sh refuses to commit a file
# matching `.env*` (other than .env.example) that contains a non-`VITE_` key.
#
# Secrets go in the deployment platform's server environment and in a password
# manager. See docs/environment.md.
# =============================================================================

# Cloudinary cloud name. Public by design — it is the host segment of every
# delivery URL (https://res.cloudinary.com/<cloud_name>/image/upload/...).
# Image delivery needs nothing else: URLs are built in src/media/cloudinary.ts
# with no SDK. The API key and secret are for uploading, which is server-only and
# not built yet.
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=yqalfmuf

# Commerce engine base URL. Left empty until the API rundown lands; unset means
# the storefront uses the fixture client (src/commerce/fixture.ts).
VITE_COMMERCE_API_BASE=
